{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1784572760,"nonce":"y2n3RYPZrMCFJAYOcVjDUWpP1S4=","title":"Implements ADR-0057 — the manual/api dispatch-reason input. Reference the ADR for locked decisions.","message":"A human dispatching a run may supply an optional free-text **reason**, which becomes the run's headline. Reuses the `trigger_title` plumbing from slice A.\n\n- `Event::Manual` and `Event::Api` gain `reason: Option\u003cString\u003e`.\n- `POST /v1/repos/{org}/{repo}/dispatch` and the inline `POST /v1/runs` accept an optional `reason: String` in the request body; it flows `DispatchRequest → Event::Manual.reason → trigger_title` (subject-style 200-char cap, for `manual`/`api` kinds). The dispatch endpoints stay dumb — accept and stamp, **no requiredness check** (enforcement is slice D).\n- The new field must NOT enter `Event::context()` (same boundary as slice A).\n- Web UI: the New-run form (`RunPipeline`) grows an optional free-text \"reason\" field; the shared Trigger cell renders the reason as the headline for manual/api runs.\n\n\n- [ ] A manual dispatch with a reason persists `trigger_title` = reason (verified via API + list DTO); a dispatch without a reason succeeds with a null headline.\n- [ ] `reason` is accepted on both `POST /dispatch` and `POST /runs`; OpenAPI regenerated + UI schema regenerated.\n- [ ] `Event::context()` does not expose `reason` (test asserts absence).\n- [ ] New-run form shows an optional reason field; a manual run shows `manual` + the reason in the Trigger cell.\n- [ ] `just check` + targeted `cargo test` green.\n\n\n- [adr-0057] Push commit-subject headline end-to-end (slice A) — provides the `trigger_title` column, extractor/stamp, DTO field, and shared Trigger-cell component.","files":null}]}